# Project conventions (radar-practice)

The canonical project guide is [`CLAUDE.md`](../../CLAUDE.md) at the repo root.
**Read it first** — it is the single source of truth for the repo map, tech
stack, conventions, skills/commands, automation, and boundaries. This file is a
thin pointer only; do not duplicate project facts here (a second copy just
drifts out of sync).

## Non-negotiable guardrails

These apply even before you open `CLAUDE.md`:

- **No PII or patient data** — no NHS numbers, patient IDs, real names, or realistic personal fixtures in prompts, code, tests, or sample data. Synthetic/redacted only.
- **Never commit or push, and never `gh pr create` / `gh pr review`, unless explicitly asked** — show changes only; the developer commits. Never force-push without instruction.
- **No stack traces or internal errors to clients** — the global exception handler returns a generic `{ error: "..." }` shape.
- **Reference-module rule** — Incidents/Audits are the structural template; Items is a demo scaffold (never a template); `legacy/` is a behaviour reference (what, not how).
- **No `any`, non-null assertions, or ESLint-rule disables** — except the documented exception in `client/src/componentRegistry.tsx`.

Everything else — repo layout, versions, testing approach, automation, data
protection detail — is in [`CLAUDE.md`](../../CLAUDE.md).
